{ "type": "Feature", "properties": { "leaf_type": "", "species": "", "species:en": "", "description": "<h1>Byrd Park Vita Course</h1><h2>Tree Tour</h2><p>This tree walk, created by Richmond Tree Stewards, features trees that are easily viewed from the path. All are mature trees with permanent labels on the trunk. Take a close look and you can find red maple flowers in very early spring, sourwood flowers in early summer, beech nuts a little later. Notice the great variety of leaf shapes and distinctive bark. There is always something to see and each season is different, so visit more than once!</p><p>Over the years many trees died or were damaged by strong storms and so, in 2009, Friends of William Byrd Park began a 3-year “Tree the Track” project. Volunteers planted and maintained 80 new trees to provide shade and beauty for walkers and runners on the park’s vita course.</p>" }, "geometry": { "type": "Point", "coordinates": [ -77.478251407949671, 37.544349878599128 ] } },
